    <string name="measure_distortion_clean">clean at every level tested</string>
    <string name="measure_distortion_quiet">distorts even at the quietest level tested</string>
    <string name="measure_distortion_up_to">clean up to %1$s dB</string>
    <string name="measure_band_line">%1$s: %2$s</string>
    <string name="measure_band_number">Band %1$d</string>
    <string name="measure_distortion_hint">Pick &quot;Measured&quot; in Speaker protection to hold each band below where it distorts.</string>
    <string name="measure_failed">The measurement failed.</string>
    <string name="measure_failed_detail">The measurement failed: %1$s</string>
    <string name="measure_permission">Measuring needs the microphone. Allow it and try again.</string>
    <string name="measure_step_1">Turn off other sound effects first (Dolby Atmos, Adapt Sound, other equalizer apps).</string>
    <string name="measure_step_2">Set media volume to a normal listening level. It\'s at %1$d%% now%2$s</string>
    <string name="measure_step_2_low">, which is probably too low.</string>
    <string name="measure_step_2_ok">.</string>
    <string name="measure_step_3">Hold the phone where your ears would be, facing the speaker. For the phone\'s own speakers, hold it as you normally do; that result is approximate, because the microphone sits next to one of them.</string>
    <string name="measure_step_4">Keep the room quiet. You\'ll hear two sweeps, about 12 seconds in all.</string>
    <string name="measure_disclaimer">Effects pause while measuring. Phone microphones aren\'t calibrated, so the correction stays gentle: at most +6 dB, and only where your speaker can play. The recording never leaves the phone.</string>
    <string name="measure_distortion_option">Also find where it starts to distort</string>
    <string name="measure_distortion_option_hint">Five more sweeps, each louder, up to full scale (about 30 seconds). It stops as soon as the speaker distorts. Use it at the volume you listen at.</string>
    <string name="measure_running">Measuring… keep quiet</string>
